    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0314" n="234" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg234"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr. Hay</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-06-02"><hi rendition="#italic">June 2,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1007.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm your
                        telegram<anchor n="a" xml:id="d195-f1"/> of the 24th ultimo and to say that
                    the Chinese Government has granted permission to the <pb facs="0315" n="235"
                        xml:id="pg235"/> United States consular officers in China to use their good
                    offices in representation of Cuba and its interests until Cuban consuls shall
                    have been appointed.</p>
                <p>I inclose copies of correspondence with the foreign office and notice to our
                    consular officers.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>




